# Cases for core-language-docs/state-space.md. Read by ../run-all.sh, which
# discovers every */CASES under snippets/ rather than carrying a list.
#
# Five pipe-separated fields:
#
#   module | cfg | expected-rc | distinct-states | what it shows
#
# A blank line or a line opening with # is skipped.
#
# THE FOURTH FIELD CARRIES MORE OF THIS PAGE THAN THE RC DOES. Three of the
# five config keywords here are state-space knobs, so their whole observable
# effect is the distinct-state count while the rc stays 0. An rc-only suite
# would be green over every one of them:
#
#   GaugeFull 6 against GaugeViewFull 2       VIEW collapses the fingerprint
#   WicketState 7 against WicketStride 4      an ACTION_CONSTRAINT cuts edges
#   Livery 8 against LiverySym 4              SYMMETRY collapses the orbit
#   Siding 4, SidingOff 4, SidingQuiet 4      one count, three exit codes
#
# The Gauge pair is the one to protect. GaugeCatch exits 12 and GaugeMiss
# exits 0 on the same spec with the same invariant, and the only difference is
# a VIEW. Its count dropping to 2 is what says the search stopped early rather
# than deciding the invariant held.
#
# Leave the field empty where the page quotes no count.
#
# Exit codes TLC uses here:
#   0    all checks passed, with a warning on stdout in two of the cases
#   10   an ASSUME in the root module is false
#   11   deadlock, meaning a reachable state with no successor
#   12   an invariant was violated by a state
#   13   an action or temporal property was violated
#   75   evaluation failed before TLC had a behavior to show
#   76   the INVARIANT slot was handed a formula that is not a state predicate
#   151  a declared invariant evaluated to FALSE with no state involved
#   255  TLC's catch-all, which is where a malformed cfg lands
#
# TWO OF THOSE CODES CARRY A SECOND MEANING, and both are the second meaning
# rather than the documented one.
#
# 151 is recorded project-wide as a cfg naming a symbol the spec does not
# define. SemaphoreFalse.cfg and RoundhouseWidth.cfg are both correct cfgs
# whose every name resolves, and both exit 151 because the declared invariant
# is constant-level and false. Filed as tla-ry2y, found first by the sets
# page's author.
#
# 76 is recorded as an invariant that could not be evaluated, with the
# behavior printed. SemaphoreSlot.cfg gets 76 for an action formula in the
# INVARIANT slot, refused before the first state with no behavior at all.

Tollgate.tla|TollgateCut.cfg|0|6|a CONSTRAINT bound, and nothing looks stuck
Tollgate.tla|TollgateSpecBound.cfg|11|6|the same bound in the spec is a dead end
